\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 One important distinction
\f1\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The formulation we settled on is 
\f0\b not trying to optimize the exact sequence directly inside the giant 800-shipment model
\f2\b0 . We first generate 
\f0\b feasible candidate tours
\f2\b0 \'97where capacity, routing, timing, windows, LIFO, compatibility, driver rules, etc. have already been checked\'97and then Gurobi chooses the cheapest combination of those tours plus LTL.
\f3\fs24 \

\f2\fs29\fsmilli14667 That gives us the core set-partitioning structure:
\f3\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \\[ \\boxed\{ \\min \\sum_k C_k^\{TL\}y_k+\\sum_iC_i^\{LTL\}z_i \} \\]\\[ \\boxed\{ \\sum_kx_\{ik\}+z_i=1 \} \\]
\f3\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 with 
\f0\b all physical and scheduling feasibility embedded in the candidate tours
\f2\b0 . This is the formulation approach we had settled on for making the main problem computationally manageable. The project also explicitly allows candidate-tour heuristics, while requiring that the final selection be done by Gurobi.
\f3\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
